xnu 0256: the real vsync selector, and a count of what the window server asks

The port's notification method was number 72 with three arguments; the
documented IOMobileFramebuffer ABI (The Apple Wiki, Dev:IOMobileFramebuffer)
has push vsync as selector 9, setVSyncNotifications(functionAddress,
userData), with the mach port coming in through IOConnectSetNotificationPort
and the async completion carrying the callback and its argument in the
reference. Implement 9 that way next to the port's own method, so a client that
asks for vsync is answered.

Nothing in the ring calls either method today, so this also counts every
selector call and prints, once a second, what the window server asked for. The
numbers say which half is missing: swapBegin/swapEnd at 60 a second with no
draw is a compositor that renders and does not present; no swapBegin at all is a
compositor that is not running; a nonzero 9 is the registration this patch
exists for.
